{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4673289","formula":"C₁₇H₂₃NO₃","hill":"C17H23NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Acetoxyketobemidone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Acetoxyketobemidone (O-Acetylketobemidone) is an opioid analgesic that is an acetylated derivative of ketobemidone. It was developed in the 1950s during research into analogues of pethidine and was assessed by the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime but was not included on the list of drugs under international control, probably because it was not used in medicine or widely available. Nevertheless, acetoxyketobemidone is controlled as an ester of ketobemidone, which is included in Schedule I of the Single Convention on Narcotic Drugs of 1961."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":23275697,"mass":289.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCC(=O)C1(CCN(CC1)C)C2=CC(=CC=C2)OC(=O)C","inchikey":"UHZAKWBTNFQWFQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"[3-(1-methyl-4-propanoylpiperidin-4-yl)phenyl] acetate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"23275697","atoms":44,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.678,"y":-0.988,"z":-0.451,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.149,"y":-0.941,"z":0.797,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.741,"y":0.905,"z":-0.515,"el":"O"},{"x":1.326,"y":3.078,"z":0.029,"el":"N"},{"x":1.596,"y":0.106,"z":-0.011,"el":"C"},{"x":1.548,"y":0.954,"z":1.288,"el":"C"},{"x":2.111,"y":1.048,"z":-1.132,"el":"C"},{"x":0.781,"y":2.273,"z":1.127,"el":"C"},{"x":1.293,"y":2.338,"z":-1.238,"el":"C"},{"x":0.292,"y":-0.607,"z":-0.399,"el":"C"},{"x":2.647,"y":-0.959,"z":0.219,"el":"C"},{"x":2.346,"y":-1.969,"z":1.31,"el":"C"},{"x":0.598,"y":4.341,"z":-0.094,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.85,"y":-0.448,"z":0.385,"el":"C"},{"x":0.251,"y":-1.415,"z":-1.536,"el":"C"},{"x":3.435,"y":-3.017,"z":1.454,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.034,"y":-1.096,"z":0.033,"el":"C